# Compose a small application

**Verify:** you can point at a cataloged module that uses each construct.

Stay on generated `@get:view` / `@post:fragment` until the next tutorials. Custom
`main.roc` is a later ownership step, not a requirement for composition.

## Components and bodies

There is no magic `children` field. Pass nested markup as a second parameter:

```rocci
@component Card = |{ title }, content|
    <section>
        <h2>{title}</h2>
        {content}
    </section>
```

Call it with a paired tag. Self-closing tags pass only props. Qualified calls
such as `<Design.Button />` use an imported module.

## Lists, conditions, variants

Use directives when branches **produce markup**:

```rocci
@if List.is_empty(items) {
    <p>Nothing yet.</p>
} else {
    <ul>
        @for item in items {
            <li>{item.label}</li>
        }
    </ul>
}

@match ({ status }) {
    Ready => <p>Ready</p>
    Failed => <p role="alert">Failed</p>
}
```

Ordinary Roc `if` / `match` belong in helpers and in `{expr}` interpolations,
not around tags. Markup is invalid inside a Roc interpolation.

`@let name = expr` binds derived data before the render items.

## Forms and names

Use `<form>` and labeled inputs. Buttons that submit mutations should say what
they do (`Increment`, `Save`). Put `role="alert"` on error text. Keyboard and
zoom are part of correctness for these examples.

The [Datastar gallery](/examples/datastar/) shows search, click-to-edit, todos,
tabs, and validation as complete source. Read those pages after this tutorial
when you want a pattern; they use custom `main.roc`, so treat them as a
preview of the later ownership tutorial.

## Assets and extra views

File-level `@css` styles the document (`body`, not `html`). Application files
under `assets/` are served from `/assets`. Additional `@get:view("/path")`
handlers are extra documents. Keep route shapes canonical (trailing slash
policy is in `rocci.toml`).

## Ability checklist

- Compose with a body parameter instead of `children`
- Choose `@if` / `@for` / `@match` for markup-producing branches
- Keep labels, buttons, and alerts meaningful
- Add a second `@get:view` without introducing `main.roc`

Next: [commands and live updates](/docs/tutorials/commands-and-live/).
